{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":["U"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{U}","name":"Unsummon","oracle_id":"837182db-1bf3-4a2c-bd01-1af9d9873561","oracle_text":"Return target creature to its owner's hand.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2026-04-24","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":["B"],"colors":["B"],"defense":null,"keywords":["Enchant"],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{B}","name":"Vampiric Link","oracle_id":"3f4521b4-1efd-4592-a50d-5ee9918df177","oracle_text":"Enchant creature\nWhenever enchanted creature deals damage, you gain that much life.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2007-02-02","toughness":null,"type_line":"Enchantment — Aura"},{"cmc":4.0,"color_identity":[],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"not_legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{4}","name":"Vedalken Orrery","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","oracle_text":"You may cast spells as though they had flash.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2022-07-08","toughness":null,"type_line":"Artifact"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"If Armadillo Cloak enchants a creature you don’t control, you’ll gain life when it deals damage, as long as that damage hasn’t already caused you to lose the game.","oracle_id":"15397a59-70a8-441f-abf7-230405a1602b","published_at":"2016-06-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"While Armadillo Cloak’s last ability is similar to lifelink, it isn’t lifelink—it’s a normal triggered ability. If a creature you control with lifelink wears an Armadillo Cloak and deals damage, first you’ll gain that much life for lifelink, and then Armadillo Cloak’s triggered ability is put onto the stack. This also means that multiple instances of Armadillo Cloak’s triggered ability do trigger separately.","oracle_id":"15397a59-70a8-441f-abf7-230405a1602b","published_at":"2016-06-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You gain life for all damage which is not prevented, regardless of what the creature damages (player or another creature) or the toughness of the blocking creature. If you put this on a 5/5 and it is blocked by a 1/1, you still gain 5 life.","oracle_id":"3f4521b4-1efd-4592-a50d-5ee9918df177","published_at":"2008-04-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The target is chosen just after any creatures dealt lethal damage at the same time that the enchanted creature dealt damage have been put into the graveyard. That might include the enchanted creature itself, if it had trample and was blocked, for example.","oracle_id":"494895db-3da1-4a19-b7a5-ea47817f4e4f","published_at":"2005-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The ability has no effect if the player has no lands.","oracle_id":"5ab62b09-1135-4d22-866b-3a0d64228bf9","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The controller of Vedalken Orrery can cast nonland artifact, creature, enchantment, and sorcery cards any time they could cast an instant. This includes on other players' turns and during the upkeep step, draw step, combat phase, and end step.","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","published_at":"2004-12-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This applies only to casting spells. It does not, for example, change when you may activate abilities that can only be activated \"any time you could cast a sorcery\".","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an attacking creature loses haste, perhaps because Fervor leaves the battlefield after attackers have been declared, it won't be removed from combat.","oracle_id":"8e0cea9c-3110-4728-9378-76849e33bb90","published_at":"2012-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Act of Treason can target any creature, even one that's untapped or one you already control.","oracle_id":"9d08af23-9f4a-4097-9abc-3b17475ab744","published_at":"2019-07-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Gaining control of a creature doesn't cause you to gain control of any Auras or Equipment attached to it.","oracle_id":"9d08af23-9f4a-4097-9abc-3b17475ab744","published_at":"2019-07-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This is not modal. If the target changes from an artifact to an enchantment or vice versa, this still destroys it.","oracle_id":"a7e97fa9-4b72-4548-b854-5be5f18a6f1a","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Choosing a creature that’s already been declared as a blocker as the target of the second mode of the activated ability won’t cause that creature to stop blocking.","oracle_id":"a9d72f78-2ab5-4e2e-ab7b-ef875e0a0609","published_at":"2024-04-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You may target a land that is already untapped with the first mode of Lost Jitte’s activated ability.","oracle_id":"a9d72f78-2ab5-4e2e-ab7b-ef875e0a0609","published_at":"2024-04-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the creature damages itself, both abilities trigger.","oracle_id":"bb81aa50-49db-4743-85fc-6b4d9ed29bc6","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The triggered ability triggers when the enchanted creature deals any damage, not only combat damage.","oracle_id":"c77ff526-c0a8-45c7-9730-2e306a0d01b8","published_at":"2022-12-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Unlike the lifelink ability, the ability of Spirit Link is a triggered ability that goes on the stack and may be responded to. Notably, if the enchanted creature deals damage at the same time you’re dealt enough damage to reduce your life total to 0 or less, you’ll lose the game before you can gain any life.","oracle_id":"c77ff526-c0a8-45c7-9730-2e306a0d01b8","published_at":"2022-12-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The last ability triggers from any damage dealt by the enchanted creature, not just combat damage.","oracle_id":"f99f44b4-a88f-403b-bbc8-bf1a45557124","published_at":"2009-02-01","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
